# Sample Recipe

File: opm/examples/recipe.oot

A recipe is a directory with a `manifest` file (key=value) and a payload. `opm ingest --from <dir>` locks it. File-backed only. No HTTP.

```
name=hello-world
version=1.2.3
origin=dir
caps=FsRead,FsWrite
license=MIT
payload=hello-world.oo
commit=
sha256=
```

## Usage

`opm ingest --from ./recipes/hello-world` reads that directory, verifies sha and caps, and writes CAS plus a v2 lock.

`opm add --from ./recipes/hello-world` installs from the same kind of directory without a registry.

Git origin (`origin=git`) needs:

```
origin=git
url=https://github.com/org/foo.git
commit=abcdef0123456789
payload=src/main.oo
sha256=
```

`commit=` must be 7+ hex digits. Not `main`, not `HEAD`. Clone uses `OODA_GIT`. Host must match `ingest.allow` or `allow=` in `ooda.pkg` (default `github.com/`). After this name is in the lock, `sha256=` is required and must match the payload.
